WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.797
The evaluator-optimizer pattern is a useful way to add bounded reflection.

00:00:05.797 --> 00:00:08.497
One component creates an output.

00:00:08.497 --> 00:00:12.872
Another component evaluates it against clear criteria.

00:00:12.872 --> 00:00:17.797
The evaluator should return structured feedback.

00:00:17.797 --> 00:00:25.427
For example: grounded is true, complete is false, citations are okay, and the missing item is order status.

00:00:25.982 --> 00:00:28.794
The controller then chooses the correction.

00:00:28.794 --> 00:00:33.019
If evidence is missing, call the appropriate tool.

00:00:33.019 --> 00:00:39.624
If evidence is complete but the wording is weak, revise the answer without retrieving again.

00:00:39.624 --> 00:00:43.104
If all criteria pass, stop.

00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:50.340
If the maximum revision count is reached, stop safely even if the evaluator is still dissatisfied.

00:00:50.839 --> 00:00:53.976
Reflection should be bounded and targeted.

00:00:53.976 --> 00:01:01.214
More passes are useful only when they can change the information, evidence, or quality of the output.
